Venetium 0016 - //build and toolchain for Windows ARM32 (target_cpu = "arm"): make the ARM graph exist.

BATCH-ARM-1 section 2, as refined by ARM-1-PLAN.md (recon of this tree) and his decisions (ARM-1-DECISIONS.md, items 1-2).
Chromium 150 has no Windows ARM32 toolchain; with target_cpu = "arm" gn gen stops at the first of a chain of asserts. 12 files:
- build/config/rust.gni: rust_abi_target thumbv7a-pc-windows-msvc for current_cpu "arm" (the std is prebuilt in rustc-rt21);
  build/rust/known-target-triples.txt: list that triple (rust.gni asserts on unknown triples).
- build/config/clang/BUILD.gn: clang_lib suffix "-arm" -> clang_rt.builtins-arm.lib (built from rt2.1's compiler-rt, s9/crt-arm).
- build/config/win/BUILD.gn: --target=arm-windows for current_cpu "arm" (CR109's one wanted hunk of this file).
- build/toolchain/win/win_toolchain_data.gni, BUILD.gn, toolchain.gni: an "arm" toolchain (win_toolchains("arm"), its data, and the
  template branch). The asm tool for arm is clang-cl --target=arm-windows -mimplicit-it=always, as arm64 uses clang-cl: the ARM
  graph's assembly is GAS-syntax .S (libvpx, webrtc, dav1d, ffmpeg), which armasm.exe cannot assemble (A2003); crashpad's one
  armasm-syntax .asm gets its own armasm step in a later patch. Windows ARM32 is Thumb-2 only, hence implicit IT blocks.
- build/toolchain/win/midl.gni: environment.arm / idl_target_platform arm32.
- build/vs_toolchain.py: CopyDlls returns early for arm (static CRT; the SDK has no Debuggers/arm/dbghelp.dll).
- build/toolchain/win/setup_toolchain.py (D9): headers from SDK 10.0.26100.0, ARM32 import libs (um/arm, ucrt/arm) from
  10.0.19041.0, the last SDK that ships them; vcvarsall otherwise points LIB at a 26100 um/arm that does not exist.
- build/config/compiler/BUILD.gn: the -march=$arm_arch ldflag only off Windows (lld-link would warn, /WX makes it an error).
- build/nocompile.gni: the arm case, so nocompile_source_set does not error for target_cpu "arm".
None of these files is in the default git index: the git diff anchor does not move; state-0016.sha256 records them.

